WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.090
&gt;&gt; CHRIS: We're headed out
to Horse Island.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.230
The Peabody has been

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:15.430
in possession of this island

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:17.110
since the early 1970s.

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.290
We're currently building

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.430
a teaching pavilion

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.210
in partnership

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.470
with the architecture school.

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.030
&gt;&gt; ALAN: He said well how about
if you guys could build a lab

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:37.800
building for us a new
building that would be

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.800
off the grid.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.570
This is the first project

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.140
of the new

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:48.460
Regenerative Building Lab at

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.060
the Yale School

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:49.750
of Architecture

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:50.350
which is a sort

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.730
of advanced version of the Yale

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.730
building project.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.840
&gt;&gt; KATIE: It was sort of a crazy
time to graduate.

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:14.020
So it worked out really
well to have this unique

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.940
but temporary project
to work on.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:17.380
&gt;&gt; LOUIS: The seminar started as
the

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.260
Regenerative Building Seminar
as a spring course.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.530
Last semester turned
into a design phase

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.180
and then ultimately now
into the construction

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:28.350
phase of the Yale Peabody
Coastal Research Center.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.180
&gt;&gt; ALAN: The idea
of this building

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:35.150
is to provide a sort of hub
for researchers

00:01:35.150 --> 00:01:38.060
who are visiting doing work
for classes coming to study

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:38.870
parts of the island.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.100
&gt;&gt; NICOLE: But of course
it's also a bit

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.240
of a balancing act, right?

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.340
Because this is a preserve
in a way and we want

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.130
to preserve it because otherwise
the research that you can

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.380
do here is not going to be
that exciting if we have

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:49.910
damaged the ecosystem too much.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.850
&gt;&gt; LOUIS: Design for disassembly
is the idea of using

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.650
screws and fasteners
which you could remove.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:56.870
So theoretically you could take
this building apart the same

00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:58.070
way that you put it together.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.600
&gt;&gt; KATIE: And because we
prefabricated so much

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:00.800
of the building on West Campus,

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.650
how we were gonna make those
components and then disassemble

00:02:03.650 --> 00:02:06.050
them and package them to be
able to rebuild them

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.419
really efficiently here
where we're lacking a lot

00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:09.620
of our tools and equipment.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:11.690
&gt;&gt; ALAN: So when the building
is ultimately

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:14.150
disassembled we can reuse
all of the materials again.

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:15.950
&gt;&gt; KATIE: I'm pretty confident
that we'll have it ready

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.300
for use in late spring.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.670
&gt;&gt; LOUIS: Every day is a fun new
problem to solve and a lot

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.520
of variety a lot
of different things.

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.980
It certainly beats the monotony
of sitting at a computer all day

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.550
long so it's it's really fun.

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.090
&gt;&gt; ALAN: As one of the guys
on the crew says

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:34.700
this is the best day of my life.
And he says it every day.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.100
So I think that's a good sign.

